From 06af0cb272572d84f75e7eb2ed70210d2c2ac0e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:19:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: render sizes 832x472 and 864x488, half-precision colour
 in the no-discard program, Data's files in subfolders

- GRAPHICS > RENDER RESOLUTION (and THPS_VITA_RES) adds 832x472 and 864x488 between 720x408
  and the screen's 960x544: t29 at 960x544 had the GPU at ~20 ms a frame (41-52 fps), 720x408
  fits 60; these are 75 and 81 percent of the screen's pixels.
- The no-discard program (opaque faces without transparent texels, most of a level) gets a
  variant with its colour maths in mediump (the texel, vertex colour and blend weight; texel
  coordinates stay highp), compiled last; rejected, the full-precision one stays.
  THPS_GL_HALF=0: not built. Boot line "[gl] half-precision colour: ...".
- Data's files at its top can move into 64 subfolders (bk00-bk63 by a hash of the name):
  opening a file in Data took 250-800 ms (t29: one sceIoOpen, ~6 ms reading), the card's
  lookup in a ~2000-file folder. Renames only, resumable (a file is in one place or the other),
  capped per start (THPS_DATA_BUCKETS_SECS, default 60); Manifest.txt's check and the
  extraction look in both places, the index searches subfolders. Off with
  THPS_DATA_BUCKETS=0 (on by default on the Vita; =undo moves them back, removing the empty
  subfolders). Tested off-device: move cut at 700 of 2000 files, resumed, run again, undo cut at
  500, finished: every listed file found at each step, contents and folder tree as at the start.
- Checked: no multisampling on the Vita (samples 0), depth D24S8 (the projective depth needs 24
  bits), atlas and layer buffers in vitaGL's graphics memory: nothing to change there.
